    "turn_text": "Welcome to Slates, I have to ask, I'm Isaac China. My guest today is Raul Grijalva, a Democratic congressman from Arizona's Third Congressional District. Born in Tucson in 1948 to Mexican immigrants, Grijalva graduated from the University of Arizona and worked in education. He was elected to the House in 2003 and is known as one of its most liberal members. He is also the co-chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus. Grijalva was the first congressman to support Bernie Sanders in last year's presidential campaign and has recently filed a lawsuit against President Trump's proposed border wall. He joins me now from Washington. So I wanted to ask you, there was a big story in the New York Times this week about divides within the Democratic Party and conflict between the left and the center of the party about how to move forward in the Trump era. As someone who's the co-chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus, this is something you must have been thinking about a lot. How concerned are you about these divides? The",
