    "turn_text": "is quite simply that part of the frustration of progressives and those of us on the left has been that our agenda, whether our economic agenda, our environmental agenda, our agenda in terms of investment, tax reform, et cetera, have always been kind of agendas that were considered problematic in terms of trying to win the center and trying to recapture the majority. And so that the concern that we would then downgrade those issues in an effort to win a full majority when it's not needed when that process of tapping down those issues is not needed or to muting those issues is not needed. Yeah, it's a concern. But I think that what has occurred particularly since the presidential primaries and what has occurred after the first 90, 100 days of Trump has been that that that voice for those issues is coming from the base. And I think if you're going to be responsive to that base, those issues are going to have to be part in parcel. Is there a part in parcel of the platform of the Democratic Party? So I'm not too concerned that those issues are going to get tapped down to the point where they become muted, because those issues are the issues that are driving people to the party. providing the energy, providing the activism, and being at the root of the",
