    "turn_text": "No, especially in the economic front. No. We're sitting here with Trump because we didn't deal with that economic front and those issues doing the presidential and He he used a fake populism that is now proving to have been a con With the American people and with voters that wanted not only changed but wanted somebody fundamentally to respond to their their issues and and it was economics so talking about jobs talking about investment talking about education and those issues are in any district that you're running for. I think they cross over those ideological lines quite easily and talking about healthcare quite easily, talking about the environment and saving public lands and climate change quite easily. And so I don't think it's a question of those issues bringing down a candidate. It's not addressing them and you can nuance it to whatever situation you feel you need to nuance it. It is a candidate, but the fundamental issue is going to be the economy and what's it doing for regular folk and for poor folk and opportunity and investment. Those are the issues that are going to carry the day in this in 2018. And I think",
