    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 94534,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94534.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I did. I think on both sides of the aisle in private conversations with my Republican colleagues and my Democratic colleagues, it is the sense of this administration's unhinged, that it doesn't have the capacity or the credibility to fully understand and govern. And so there's a there's trepidation on both sides. What's next? And what further damage can that can this administration do not only to to the institutions in our democracy but more importantly or just as importantly to the American people as a whole because some of the damage that's being done just through administrative action are generational is going to take a while. For us to undo that damage and and I think that the word trepidation a little bit of fear and Just that it's unhinged and since it has no capacity and it's lost its credibility It's in a dangerous time",
