  {
    "episode_id": 94534,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94534.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "I think the, you know, Arizona was the petri dish of what anti-immigrant law can we put in place and beginning with 1070. But I think what occurred and there's a moment in history, you can kind of pinpoint it. It was when the dreamers made their case public when you started to see those young faces when they took that risk that the conversation around immigration started to change. And it started to change because suddenly there was a person attached to it. It wasn't a fundamental, you know, you couldn't You couldn't just rhetorically say, oh, there are criminals. All of a sudden, you had a whole different situation in front of you. And I think the same is occurring right now that you cannot categorically make the kind of statements that Trump has made without that catching up with you. And so now you see families. Now you see moms, now you see citizen children in foster care because their parents have been deported. And so you begin to humanize it, for lack of a better word. And I think what happened in Arizona, once it became humanized, then that's when our pile got defeated. Once the extremists were isolated for what they were, and once you peel away all the layers of justification, you're left with a group that is fundamentally racist. supremacist and they don't have the cache nor nor do they have the appeal with regular folk across Arizona and I think I believe across this country. Trump did a good job of creating fear and blame on the immigrant community for everybody else's situation and I think that is catching up with him too but hopefully that humanization process is much more rapid than it was around the dreamers, because we had, you know, took a while to convince President Obama that that was the right executive order to do. And once it's done, it's an executive order that even Trump isn't afraid to touch.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
